              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the French for the watchmaker, then the French for the jeweller."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: le fleuriste",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "le fleuriste — \"the florist\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Le fleuriste a fait un joli bouquet pour ma mère. The florist made a pretty bunch of flowers for my mother."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Same form for a woman: la fleuriste."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "fleuriste is built on fleur 'flower' with -iste; fleur is inherited from Latin flōs, flōris (EtymDB)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
            }
          ]
        },
